Semantic elements: are HTML tags that clearly describe the meaning and purpose of their content 
to browsers, developers, and search engines.
Advantages: 
1) Better Readability - Developers can quickly locate different parts of the page.
                        Makes code easier to understand and maintain.
2) Improves SEO - Search engines can better understand the webpage structure.
3) Better Accessibility - Screen readers can identify page sections easily. Improves user experience for visually disabled users.
4) Browser Understanding - Browsers can interpret the content more meaningfully. 
Browser can better support accessibility tools, help search engines identify important content, improve page structure interpretation

Advantages of HTML5 Input Types:
1) Built-in Validation - Browser automatically validates data. Example: email, url.
2) Better User Experience - Date pickers, color pickers, sliders are provided automatically.
3) Mobile-Friendly - Mobile devices show appropriate keyboards. Example: type="email" → Email keyboard type="tel" → Numeric keypad
4) Improved Accessibility - Browsers understand the expected input type and screen readers reads onput types like Number edit field.






stateless components or presentational components --- components do not manage, update or track their internal state.
core features:
  1) No internal state - They do not use useState or this.state
  2) No side effects - No data fetching and leaves state logic to statefull container.
  3) Predictable & pure - They act as pure functions with same props. They will always render exact same UI output.
  4) Driven by props - They receive data from their parent component through props and render it directly.
Advantages:
  1) Reusability - Easy to reuse across different parts of application ( No dependent with any side effects).
  2) Performance - Light weight execution because they do not track life cycle hooks and state updates.
  3) Easier Testing - Simple to write unit test cases because there is no complex state updates or side effects.

When component re-renders
  1) State Updates - Modifying state with useState ( setter function).
  2) prop changes - Receiving new data from parent components.
  3) Context changes - Consumed context values changes.
  4) Parent re-renders - Child component re-renders when parent component re-renders.

Differences between class component and functional component
  1) syntax - functional components are plain Javascript functions. class components extend React.Component.
  2) state -  functional components use useState hook and class components uses this.state.
  3) Life cycle - functional components handles with useEffect hook and  class components
                  life cycle methods like componentDidMount, componentDidUpdate and componentWillUnmount
  4) This keyword - functional components do not use this and class components heavily depends on this and require method binding.
  Why functional components prefered:
  1) Less boilerplate - cleaner, shorter and easier code to read and maintain.
  2) Logic reuse - custom hooks allow sharing statefull logic between components easily.
  3) Performance - Avoids performance issue and memory issue creating class insances.
  4) Easier testing - easy to write test cases.
  5) Cleaner life cycle Logic - useEffect groups related logic instead of splitting into multiple life cycle methods.

React Fragments - Fragments is a feature that allows you to group multiple child elements together without 
                  adding extra DOM nodes into the browser real DOM.
  1) Syntax - short form <> </>   Long form <React.Fragment> </React.Fragment>
  2) No extra DOM Nodes - fragments do not renders into the final HTML output.
  3) Maintains HTML structure - ex:- bad syntax with div <td> <div> </div> </td> fragments resolve this issues.
  4) Keep CSS without breaking - extra div may break existing CSS like css flex box and grid. 
  5) Performance - By reducing the no of nested DOM Nodes, applicstions use less memory and faster in rendering.
  6) Key prop execution - when using key prop then use <React.Fragment key={ID}>


    
